zen-lab-accelerate = Accelerate growth x2
zen-lab-accelerate-tooltip = Double growth speed. Instability +0.9/s, temperature +0.4 C/s. Grow at least half the sample in this mode to earn a second breakthrough. Thermal runaway starts at 75% instability.
zen-lab-accelerated-started = Accelerated growth enabled. The reaction becomes self-sustaining at 75% instability.
zen-lab-accelerated-growing = Accelerated growth: double speed. Instability and temperature are rising.
zen-lab-growth-reward = Additional breakthrough: { $progress }%. Grow half the sample in accelerated mode for the reward. Thermal runaway starts at 75% instability.
zen-lab-runaway-started = The reaction is self-sustaining. The cooler only lowers temperature. To save the sample, stop the apparatus, open the lid and apply stabilizer while exposed to discharges. Alternatively, quench the sample.
zen-lab-runaway-status = [color=#EF8276]THERMAL RUNAWAY. Stabilizer through an open lid and cooling are required: instability <=60%, temperature <=35 C. The cooler does NOT reduce instability! At 100% a breach countdown begins.[/color]
zen-lab-breach-countdown = [color=#FF6257]BREACH IN { $seconds } s. Use stabilizer to reduce instability below 85%, or quench the sample. The cooler does NOT stop the countdown! Opening the lid is dangerous; a closed lid will not prevent a breach.[/color]
zen-lab-countdown-cancelled = Breach countdown cancelled. The reaction continues: use stabilizer to reduce instability to 60% and the cooler to reach 35 C. Cooling alone is insufficient.
zen-lab-containment-cooling = Cooling: -2.5 C/s. Instability is NOT reduced. The reaction adds +1.5 C/s and +1/s. To apply stabilizer, stop the apparatus and open the lid; beware of discharges.
zen-lab-contained = Thermal runaway contained. Growth paused; select a mode to resume. The current task is preserved.
zen-lab-runaway-apparatus = During runaway, the cooler is the only permitted apparatus. It lowers temperature, but stopping the reaction requires stabilizer through an open lid.
zen-lab-lid-vent = DANGER: opening the chamber released a thermal discharge. Close the lid! An exposed unstable sample burns nearby personnel.
zen-lab-breach-finished = Local Xen breach! Sample destroyed, laboratory equipment damaged. Burns and electric shock within three meters. Two headcrabs and a houndeye have appeared.
zen-lab-quench = Emergency quench: destroy sample
zen-lab-quench-confirm = Confirm sample destruction
zen-lab-quench-tooltip = Irreversibly destroys the sample and all progress, with no breakthroughs awarded. Stops runaway and the breach countdown. Without power, use the chamber context menu.
zen-lab-quenched = Sample irreversibly quenched. Breach prevented, research reward lost. The residue can only be recycled.
zen-lab-quench-author = Performed an emergency sample quench.
zen-lab-bonus-announcement = Research of an accelerated-growth Xen crystal is complete. The station received 2 scientific breakthroughs for crew upgrades.
zen-lab-research-bonus-finished = Research complete. Accelerated growth earned 2 scientific breakthroughs. The sample is ready for the resonator.
